WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.710
Each year, about 90,000
people from around Cusco,

2
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.710
in Peru, make a pilgrimage
to the Sinakara hollow.

3
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:12.210
They carry processions of crosses
up and down a snow-capped mountain.

4
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:17.730
In the Swiss Alps, hydropower supplies
about 58.5 per cent of Swiss electricity,

5
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.770
on a ten-year average.

6
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:25.210
And on the Arctic tundra, Saami reindeer
herders graze their herds in summer.

7
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.970
Power, pasture, pilgrimage.

8
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.770
So should these landscapes
be used, or left alone?

9
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:36.330
In this mission, you'll sort the
values a glaciated landscape holds:

10
00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.990
environmental, cultural and economic.

11
00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.810
Then you'll travel from Swiss
dams to Yosemite's wilderness,

12
00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:45.550
and find out why the
tundra matters for carbon.

13
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:49.330
Your mission: decide whether
glaciated landscapes should be used,

14
00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:50.760
or left alone.
